tests:
  unit:
    waived: "measurement-only WU - produces recorded numbers and a corpus, changes no code. The diff is two T3 docs (plan, result) and nothing else; git diff --name-only over base..tip touches no src/, xtask/, tests/, ui/src/ or ui/e2e/ path, so there is no function added or changed for a unit test to cover. Pre-registered in the epic plan's E2E test plan in this exact wording."
  integration:
    waived: "measurement-only WU - produces recorded numbers and a corpus, changes no code. W2 adds no mechanism with a bounded contract: the replay is a procedure an agent session executes, not code that ships. Same pre-registration."
  e2e:
    waived: "Epic-level, not WU-level. The epic's e2e is a full review run under the adopted configuration asserting verdict parity against the baseline sweep; W2 produces the baseline half of that comparison and adopts no configuration, so it cannot carry the flow."
verified:
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc green on docs/work/2026-09-07-crscope-w2-plan.html (wu-plan) and docs/work/2026-09-07-crscope-w2-result.html (wu-result)."
  - "Reproducibility check 1 of 4 (pinned scopes): all three timed entries recorded as full base and head SHAs plus the diff_sha256 their historical cr note carries - 083fda7e6fc8, 7caf7b49148f, ecd22bb53edd. A re-runner can prove they measured the same bytes."
  - "Reproducibility check 2 of 4 (self-reported timings): FAILED AS SPECIFIED, and this is why the plan demanded both clocks. Five of 106 roles reported an END later than the orchestrator's wall clock at the moment their result arrived - impossible, not merely doubtful; one claimed 575 s where the harness measured 223 s. Every figure in the result is the harness's own duration. The rule is recorded because a role that mis-transcribes its own clock cannot be caught from inside its own report."
  - "Reproducibility check 3 of 4 (n stated per figure): the complex band's verify and verified-recall figures are labeled n=2 in every table; its find figures are n=3. No single-run number is presented as a baseline."
  - "Reproducibility check 4 of 4 (deviations declared): eight, and the enumeration matches the result's deviations table row for row - (1) the design probe never ran, (2) complex verify is n=2, (3) self-reported role clocks proved unreliable and the harness clock is authoritative, (4) three solo calibration probes excluded, (5) sections 2 and 6 omitted from every replay, (6) cr notes withheld from every role, (7) the rubric pinned to this tip's blob 755e70bc, (8) identical claims from two finders counted as one candidate. Rows 1 and 2 are the two shortfalls below. Cold replay targets are a property of the replay environment, recorded in the result's evidence table - they are not a deviation, and an earlier version of this check wrongly counted them as one in place of row 3."
  - "106 roles returned: 45 finders across 9 complete find phases (5 each), 58 verifiers across 8 complete verify phases (9/11/11 simple, 8/3/2 moderate, 8/5/1 complex), 3 calibration probes; a further 6 verifiers were killed by the rate limit. Every per-role duration is in the result's appendix, which is the primary record - the session log does not outlive the session."
  - "Every derived figure is recomputable from that appendix rather than carried from the session log, and the recomputation was run: the pooled verifier medians are 89 s (simple, 31 values), 90 s (moderate, 13) and 111 s (complex, 14 - the mean of the two middle values, the convention now stated in the document). Review round 2 found three of them wrong and the find/verify ratio claim false against the phase table; all four are corrected on this tip."
  - "Verdict parity held 8 of 8 against the historical notes (all FAIL), which the result records as a weak instrument rather than a pass: it held while recall was 0/5."
waived_layers_replaced_by: "The plan required reproducibility of the measurement in place of a suite, in four numbered checks. Three passed. Check 2 failed and the failure is reported as a finding about the instrument, with the authoritative clock named. Check 4's own enumeration was found miscounted in review round 2 and is corrected here - the check is only worth its place if it is itself checkable."
note: "TWO SHORTFALLS, stated as shortfalls. A session API rate limit (HTTP 429) killed complex run 3's verify phase mid-flight - six of seven verifiers died, one returned - so the complex band carries n=2 for verify. And the design probe (42875df5..9b16798c, n=3 find-only) never ran, so the section 3b design finder has NO baseline, which is exactly what plan v2's amendment existed to deliver. The rate limit is only the second cause of that one: the probe was 18 roles against the bands' 109 and was scheduled last, so the cheapest plan-mandated deliverable was the one certain to be lost first, and the deviation now says so. Neither shortfall is re-scoped away; both are follow-ups 1 and 2 in the result. What did complete: simple n=3 whole, moderate n=3 whole, complex r1 and r2 whole plus r3's find phase whole. The substantive results do not depend on the missing runs - recall was 0/5 on the moderate band in all three of its complete runs, and the verdict flips are counted only over judgements that actually returned."
